{
  "title": "Model Settings",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9f76871f34575ab1",
      "text": "Which model the Plan Tool asks when it uses one: ✎ Revise Plan, ⧉ Revise Site and Go Ahead. Opened from the ⚙ chip on a plan's status line; the choice is kept in this browser, for this site."
    },
    {
      "type": "plan",
      "id": "0fe8ce266a669cbb",
      "text": "MODELS"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "f060751a1e43b74d",
      "text": "# Changing Model"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "4c8a4897e6691488",
      "text": "> Each run is one request, so a change costs nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "6607e789bc0d4d8b",
      "text": "The Plan Tool keeps no conversation with a model. Every run builds its question afresh from the pages — the plan, its answered questions, the skills it names and the pages it links, up to 120 kB — and sends it whole. Changing model between runs therefore loads nothing extra into the new one: the next run sends what it would have sent anyway. The warning in the Claude app is about a long chat, whose whole history must be read again, uncached, by the new model; there is no such history here."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "b8a16ed453fc7017",
      "text": "What does matter is the window. A plan's question is often 20–35 thousand tokens. The coop's big models (GLM-5.3 Flash, DeepSeek-V4) and Claude hold that easily; the 32K models and Ollama only just, or not at all. A model too small for the question is refused before anything is sent, with the sizes, rather than answering from a plan cut short."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "f03094752b9755e7",
      "text": "# Defaults"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "0fda2ee9ac7a8543",
      "text": "> The coop first; Claude when the work needs it."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "b10c9c62b31cbbde",
      "text": "Farm default means the farm's PLAN_MODEL, else the coop's auto-big, which uses whichever big model is already loaded on its GPUs. Choose a Claude model for a redraft that needs careful reasoning (Claude Fable 5.1 is the strongest), or Auto to let the farm decide each run. ⌕ Red-link always uses Claude, because only Claude has web search here."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "bb269957bfcd7279",
      "text": "# Auto\n> Claude for the big runs; the coop's own routing for the rest."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "64832fa151a575f6",
      "text": "With Auto chosen, every ✎ Revise Plan, ⧉ Revise Site and each page of Go Ahead is weighed before it is sent: the size of its question in tokens, the answered questions that go in, the open phases a redraft may change, and for Go Ahead the row's action and whether it is the plan. A big run goes to Claude Fable 5.1: a question over 48 thousand tokens, four answers or more, a whole site, a page or the plan that Go Ahead rewrites, or a redraft heavy with answers and open phases. Everything smaller goes to the coop's auto-big, which picks the model for its own hardware. A question too big for Claude's window goes to the coop's roomiest model; a small one the coop cannot take, or a coop that does not answer, goes to Claude, and the reason says so."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "45a47dc7fa28659c",
      "text": "The rule is fixed, not a model's guess, so the same run always picks the same model, and choosing costs nothing. The status line names the pick and why, for example *auto → auto-big: 9k tokens, 2 answers (routes to glm-5.3-flash-pp)* or *auto → claude-fable-5-1 (big): 52k tokens, 5 answers*. The farm can name another Claude model in PLAN_AUTO_BIG, another coop router in PLAN_AUTO_LIGHT, and move the 48 thousand token line with PLAN_AUTO_BIG_TOKENS."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "fac5064a9816cd15",
      "text": "# See"
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "c346c9c2a99e119b",
      "text": "- [[Plan Tool]]\n- [[About Plan Plugin]]"
    }
  ],
